"I saw my parents cry with joy at having been given the opportunity to vote, but now we're getting stuck," he said.
Although they got a narrow but important, victory in the regional elections last December, the Catalan independence parties have struggled to maintain momentum, and many of their well-known executives have either moved into exile themselves or sitting in detention, awaiting verdict for their role in holding the vote and the ensuing declaration of independence.
