But the primary goal of this streak of voter rallies is to create the momentum of the Republicans who are facing a difficult election in November.
Figures from President Trump's campaign team said the five voter rallies next week aim to "encourage energy among volunteers and backers when Republicans are trying to protect and deepen the majorities they have in the Senate and the House of Representatives."
"Control over Congress is as important for his agenda that the president will travel to as many states as possible, now that we are stepping into the bustling campaign time," a spokesperson for the Trump campaign, who wouldn't be cited by name.
