Saturday will be the second time in the past month, Trump has visited West Virginia, the state, he won by over 40 percentage points in 2016.
Trump is attempting to help West Virginia's Republican nominee to the Senate, Patrick Morrisey, who is lagging behind in the polls.
"That's not a good sign for Morrisey that the president has to troop up to give him a boost in the polls," Simon Haeder, who is dealing with political science at West Virginia University.
Ryder Cup 2018: Team U.S. has shown fighting spirit and trying to keep hope alive ahead of Sunday's single duels
After three one-sided laps, Saturday's four-man duels were perhaps what this Ryder Cup needed.
The fluctuating momentum pendulum is a thoroughly invented sports concept, but a concept that the players believe in – not least at competitions like this.
So where would they say there's momentum now?
"They waged by six points, and now it's four, so we'll probably see that a bit as momentum," Jordan Spieth said.
Of course, Europe has the advantage. They are 4 points in front and there are 12 points more to play about.
As Spieth says, however, the Americans feel they've got a bit of wind in the sails, and there's plenty of encouraging things to focus on, not least the form at Spieth and Justin Thomas, who played together all day and both can boast three points of four possible.
