China announced a 14% surge in the number of citizens with HIV and AIDS.
More than 82,20,000 people in the country are affected," health authorities said.
In the second-quarter of 2018 alone, 40,000 new cases were recorded.
The vast majority of the new cases were sexually transmissible, which is a new trend.
Vigorously, HIV spread quickly in some parts of China due to infected blood transfusions.
"However, the number of people getting HIV in this way has been reduced to somewhat near-zero-nezed Chinese health authorities at a conference in Yunnanprovinsen.
